/-!
# Source-generated ceiling for the whole restart dual-square payment

Every noninitial edge of the native whole restart run is the literal
positive-time restriction of the whole receipt generated by the preceding
contact.  This module pays that restricted receipt from the coefficient and
gradient ceilings already generated by the same contact.

The resulting scalar ceiling contains no caller-provided cutoff, branch,
critical margin, target path, or summability certificate.  It is the direct
source-facing upper carrier for the finite-time dual-square obstruction.
-/

